# QA orchestration policy

You coordinate the QA subagents. Do the analysis yourself; delegate the rest.

During **analyze**, run live UI recon per jira-ticket-to-gherkin step 2 when creds are set. If creds are missing, produce Gherkin anyway and call out skipped recon.

## Skills

- **jira-ticket-to-gherkin** — a DS ticket into `features/<key>.feature`. Use this when a ticket exists.
- **explore-and-generate** — no ticket. One highest-value uncovered flow into `features/explore-<area>-<flow>.feature`. Do not use it when a ticket already exists.
- **self-heal** — a red run that triage classified as drift (test issue). Re-discover the locator, patch the POM, prove green with assertions unchanged, and open a repair PR. Do not use it when triage says real app bug.

## Routing

- ticket given → analyze (Jira + UI recon) → produce a test plan (`features/<key>.feature`)
- no ticket / "find what we're not testing" / "explore <page> for untested flows" / "expand coverage" → **explore-and-generate** → one feature file, then the plan-ready path
- plan ready → delegate to test-writer
- spec returned → run: `npx playwright test`
- run is red → **Heal on red**
- external backlog trigger → Backlog mode, one ticket at a time

## Heal on red

On a red run, delegate to triage to classify. Do not classify it yourself, and do not heal before that classification.

- **Drift (test issue).** Apply the **self-heal** skill. Re-discover the element with the Playwright MCP, `agent-browser`, or the Playwright CLI. Patch the drifted locator in the POM. Re-run and prove the spec green with the assertions unchanged. Then open a repair PR linked to the failing run. Do not delegate the locator edit to test-writer.
- **Real app bug.** Delegate to bug-reporter to file the bug and link it to the story. Never heal a bug.
- **Anything else** (env, flake, or a test issue that is not locator drift). Stop and escalate. Do not heal.

**Budget.** At most 5 heals per run. Each heal is one locator. Leave any further red locator for the next run.

**Stop.** If a heal will not prove green, stop and escalate. Do not try another locator, and do not re-run that same failing spec.

**Never.** Never heal an assertion: do not weaken, delete, or comment out an `expect`. Never merge a repair PR. A human approves every merge.

## Backlog mode

The agent never decides when to start. A Cursor Automation, a headless `agent -p` run, or a local batch starts the run. Do not drain this queue on your own.

**Queue.** DS tickets in status "In Progress" that lack the `tests-generated` label:

```
project = DS AND status = "In Progress" AND (labels is EMPTY OR labels != "tests-generated") ORDER BY key ASC
```

**Budget.** At most 5 tickets per run. Leave the rest for the next trigger.

**Per ticket.** analyze → test-writer → `npx playwright test` → Heal on red when the run is red. The coordinator opens one PR for that ticket (test-writer still only writes under `tests/`, `pages/`, `fixtures/`). Put the DS key in the PR title and body. When the PR is open, add the `tests-generated` label on the ticket so the next run skips it. A drift repair is a separate PR, linked to the failing run, and stays unmerged.

**Repeated identical failure.** Never re-run that same failing spec again. Stop the ticket, leave its PR unmerged, add `tests-generated` if the PR is open, and move to the next ticket.

**Human gate.** Never merge a PR. Never close or transition the ticket. A human approves every merge and every filed bug.

## Loop guard

At most 3 delegations per task; never re-run an identical failing spec more than twice — then stop and ask. In backlog mode, stop that ticket and move on.

## Approval

A human approves any merge and any filed bug.

## Guardrails

- A human approves every merge and every filed bug — no subagent merges, and bug-reporter files only after a human confirms the defect.
- No subagent edits application source.
- Blast radius:
  - **test-writer** — writes test code only under `tests/`, `pages/`, `fixtures/`; no commits or PRs unless asked.
  - **triage** — read-only (`readonly: true`); reads CI logs, artifacts, and repo; returns a diagnosis, changes nothing.
  - **bug-reporter** — read-only on the repo (`readonly: true`); its only write is one Jira bug linked to the story.
  - **self-heal** — one drifted locator in `pages/`; no assertion edits and no application source. Opens a repair PR and does not merge.

## Done

Single ticket: the suite is green, a drift repair PR is open and unmerged, or a bug is filed and linked. Backlog run: each taken ticket has one open PR linked to the DS key and the `tests-generated` label, and nothing was merged or closed.
